    "result_text": "The change is complete and both acceptance tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented client contacts as a full-stack, additive change following the project's existing patterns (modeled on the client\u2192projects sub-resource).\n\n**Database** \u2014 `V9__contacts.sql`: a new `contacts` table (`id`, `client_id` FK \u2192 clients, `name`, `email`, `role`), using `GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY` so test-seed fixtures can insert explicit ids.\n\n**Server** (OfficeFloor REST, new `contact` package):\n- `Contact` entity, `ContactRepository`, `ContactView`, `NewContact` request body\n- `ListClientContacts` \u2192 `GET /api/clients/{id}/contacts` (ordered by id)\n- `CreateContact` \u2192 `POST /api/clients/{id}/contacts` (validates name/email/role, sets clientId from the path)\n- Two new YAML endpoint files under `rest/api/clients/{id}/`\n\n**Test support** \u2014 extended `TestSupportController`: seeds a `contacts` fixture array (via `JdbcTemplate` with explicit ids) and adds `contacts` to the `TRUNCATE ... RESTART IDENTITY` reset.\n\n**Front-end** \u2014 added a `ClientContacts` component inside the existing clients feature (contacts belong to the client's page, so the code stays with that feature). It renders on the opened client with the `data-testid` anchors the spec requires: `client-contacts-table`, `contact-row-<id>`, `contact-name`/`contact-email`/`contact-role`, plus the add form (`contact-form-name/email/role/submit`).\n\nNo pinned scaffolding, CLAUDE.md, or the test spec were touched. The spec asserts no audit records for this feature, so none were added.",
